        <description>&lt;p&gt;The agent&amp;#x27;s own home, hosted — and plugins.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Added&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;**The agent on the Spire home**: Spire now starts the installed Hermes Agent&amp;#x27;s own dashboard and hosts it right on the home page — chat, sessions, profiles, models, all of Hermes&amp;#x27;s own surfaces in Spire&amp;#x27;s window. Spire supervises the process and provides the window; it builds none of what&amp;#x27;s inside.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;**Plugins**: Spire gains a plugin structure mirroring Hermes&amp;#x27;s own — one folder per plugin in Spire&amp;#x27;s data directory with a small manifest, all data, never code changes. Hermes is the first plugin; its manifest declares how it runs and what it provides, and you can edit it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item>
